---
import PublicLayout from '../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';
---

<PublicLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions | St. Paul's Mission Hospital"
  description="Terms and conditions governing use of the St. Paul's Mission Hospital careers and recruitment portal."
  canonicalPath='/terms'>
  <section class='border-b border-[var(--color-border-soft)]'>
    <div class='max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-10 pt-20 sm:pt-28 pb-12 sm:pb-16'>
      <p
        class='text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-[var(--color-brand)] mb-5'>
        Legal
      </p>
      <h1
        class='text-[2rem] sm:text-4xl font-black tracking-[-0.025em] leading-[1.1] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-6'>
        Terms &amp; conditions.
      </h1>
      <p class='text-[15px] text-gray-600 leading-[1.75]'>
        These terms govern your use of the recruitment portal at
        <span class='font-mono text-[13px]'>recruitment.spmh.co.ke</span> and any
        associated services operated by St. Paul's Mission Hospital.
      </p>
      <p class='text-[12px] text-gray-400 mt-4 italic'>
        Effective date: 1 January 2026 · Version 1.0
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class='bg-white'>
    <div class='max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-10 py-16 sm:py-20'>
      <div class='prose-legal'>
        <h2>1. Acceptance of terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing or using this portal, you agree to be bound by these
          terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the portal. We may
          update these terms from time to time; continued use after an update
          constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Purpose of the portal</h2>
        <p>
          This portal is operated by St. Paul's Mission Hospital to publish
          employment opportunities and to receive applications from candidates.
          It is not a public marketplace and is not intended for any purpose
          other than recruitment.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Eligibility</h2>
        <p>
          You may apply for positions through this portal if you are legally
          eligible to work in the Republic of Kenya and can provide the
          documentation required for the role. Where a specific position
          requires professional registration, you are responsible for
          maintaining a valid licence.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Accuracy of information</h2>
        <p>
          You agree that all information you submit is true, complete, and
          accurate. Providing false, misleading, or incomplete information —
          including in your CV, cover letter, or any supporting document — may
          result in your application being rejected, or — if discovered after
          hire — in termination of employment.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Submissions and intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          By submitting an application, you grant St. Paul's Mission Hospital
          the right to store, process, and review the information and documents
          you provide, solely for the purpose of recruitment. You retain
          ownership of your content; the hospital does not acquire any rights
          beyond what is necessary for the recruitment process.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Personal data</h2>
        <p>
          Personal data submitted through the portal is processed in accordance
          with the hospital's Privacy Notice and the Kenya Data Protection Act,
          2019. Please read the Privacy Notice before submitting an application.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Submit false, misleading, or fraudulent information.</li>
          <li>
            Upload files that contain viruses, malware, or malicious code.
          </li>
          <li>
            Attempt to access the portal's administrative areas without
            authorisation.
          </li>
          <li>Scrape, harvest, or otherwise collect data about other users.</li>
          <li>Use the portal to harass, threaten, or defame any person.</li>
          <li>
            Interfere with the normal operation of the portal or its
            infrastructure.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. No guarantee of employment</h2>
        <p>
          Submitting an application through this portal does not create an
          employment relationship, an offer of employment, or any obligation on
          the part of St. Paul's Mission Hospital. Only a written offer signed
          by an authorised representative of the hospital constitutes an offer
          of employment.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Availability of the portal</h2>
        <p>
          We aim to keep the portal available at all times but do not guarantee
          uninterrupted access. The portal may be unavailable during
          maintenance, updates, or circumstances beyond our control. We are not
          liable for any loss arising from unavailability.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          The portal relies on third-party infrastructure and services for
          hosting, email delivery, and secure data storage. We select our
          providers carefully but are not responsible for their independent acts
          or omissions.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, St. Paul's Mission Hospital
          shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential
          loss arising out of or in connection with your use of the portal.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Kenya. Any
          dispute arising in connection with these terms shall be subject to the
          exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Kenya.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms may be directed to the Human Resources
          Department at
          <a href='mailto:recruitment@spmh.co.ke'>recruitment@spmh.co.ke</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PublicLayout>

<style>
  .prose-legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .prose-legal h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .prose-legal p {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #4b5563;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }
  .prose-legal ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }
  .prose-legal ul li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.35rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #4b5563;
  }
  .prose-legal ul li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.6rem;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--color-brand);
  }
  .prose-legal a {
    color: var(--color-brand);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
